* libedhoc — MIT License
  Location : components/routeloom/third_party/libedhoc/ (LICENSE)
  Copyright: (c) 2024, Kamil Kiełbasa and others
  Upstream : https://github.com/kamil-kielbasa/libedhoc
  Version  : v2.3.2, commit c8857b62d66be3664d1694bbe4eea37c56c05d9e (the
             pin fixed in docs/design/host-security-readiness/
             05-production-security.md §1)
  Notes    : EDHOC (RFC 9528) protocol engine of the SDK v1 join/link
             handshakes (docs/design/sdk-v1/08 P2-1). Subset: include/,
             library/core/, library/internal/, backends/{cbor,memory,log}/;
             upstream's PSA reference cipher suites, tests, Zephyr and CMake
             files are not vendored. Local patches enforce exact message decode
             lengths and one-byte connection-ID compaction (blob ids and
             upstream transformations in
             components/routeloom/third_party/VENDORED.json, checked by
             tests/test_vendored_sources.py); RouteLoom's configuration and
             crypto/memory/credential backend are RouteLoom code in
             components/routeloom/src/edhoc/. The MIT notice in LICENSE must
             accompany source and binary redistributions.

* zcbor — Apache License 2.0
  Location : components/routeloom/third_party/zcbor/ (LICENSE)
  Copyright: Nordic Semiconductor ASA
  Upstream : https://github.com/NordicSemiconductor/zcbor
  Version  : 0.8.1, commit d3093b5684f62268c7f27f8a5079f166772619de (the
             externals/zcbor submodule pin of the libedhoc commit above)
  Notes    : CBOR runtime (include/, src/) that libedhoc's generated CBOR
             backend is built against, compiled with ZCBOR_CANONICAL.
             src/zcbor_encode.c has one local guard to skip a zero-byte
             memmove when libedhoc supplies a null empty protected header.
             VENDORED.json records the upstream and patched blob ids;
             tests verify the exact one-line transformation. No NOTICE
             file upstream.

* TF-PSA-Crypto (Mbed TLS crypto) — Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-or-later,
  used here under Apache-2.0
  Location : components/routeloom/third_party/tf-psa-crypto/ (LICENSE)
  Copyright: The Mbed TLS Contributors
  Upstream : https://github.com/Mbed-TLS/TF-PSA-Crypto
  Version  : 1.1.0, commit 29160dd877d29658279fd683b2ae57b320ddcf09 (the
             tf-psa-crypto submodule of Mbed TLS commit
             0fe989b6b514192783c469039edd325fd0989806, which is libedhoc's
             externals/mbedtls pin)
  Notes    : Only the builtin AES block cipher and the CCM and GCM
             modes plus the headers they include, configured by
             components/routeloom/src/edhoc/tf_psa_crypto_config.h. Provides
             the AES-CCM-16-64-128 of EDHOC cipher suite 2 and the
             AES-GCM-128 of the SDK v1 authority channel in HOST builds
             only; the ESP-IDF component does not compile it (firmware uses
             ESP-IDF's own Mbed TLS through PSA). Unmodified.

